        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Who Should Buy the Blitz</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Buy the Blitz if</strong> you train for speed and power — field sports, sprinting,
            combat sports or conditioning — and want one machine that sprints, resists and pushes like a
            sled; if you weigh more than the 330 to 350 lb that cheaper curved trainers allow; or if you
            are already buying a Bells of Steel rack and like the idea of one freight delivery and one
            supplier.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Look elsewhere if</strong> you mostly run at a steady pace (a shallower curve or a
            motorized treadmill will be more comfortable), if you mainly walk (see our
            <a href="/manual-vs-motorized-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">manual vs motorized comparison</a>),
            or if price matters, since the SOLE C80 delivers resisted curved running for about half the
            money. And if you live upstairs, Bells of Steel's own advice is to install it on a ground floor.
          </p>
        </div>

